  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nLow pressure continues to pull away, but a weak inverted trof is\nkeeping an area of rain/showers persistent over parts of the\nwestern Maine mtns into the lower Androscoggin Valley. That\nshould continue into the early morning hours before forcing\ndrifts too far east.\n\nAfter that it will be largely dry thru the midpoint of the\nweekend. There is really only the threat of isolated to widely\nscattered showers or thunderstorms today and Sat afternoons. \n\nThe next best chance of rain looks like late Sun into Mon. A\nslow moving frontal boundary will cross the region. At this time\nensemble guidance is showing plenty of members indicating\nappreciable rainfall, but this would not be the first time this\nwarm season the rug has been pulled at the last minute. I do\nthink precip is likely, but the amounts I will lean more\nconservative. Timing also looks like we avoid peak surface based\ninstability, so the threat for severe weather is relatively\nlow. \n\nTemps overall thru the middle part of the next week look\nseasonable, though Sun night and maybe Mon night overnight\nreadings could be on the mild and muggy side.",
